§ `VerifyVacuousGuardFixture`

-- Negative control: a guard that excludes nothing.
--
-- `x OR y` is already entailed by the `x` it is conjoined with, so the second
-- clause never rules anybody out. A reader would take it for a second hurdle;
-- it is not one.

GIVEN x IS A BOOLEAN
      y IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the second hurdle is not one` IS
  x AND (x OR y)
